---
import BaseLayoutV2 from '../layouts/BaseLayoutV2.astro';
import ProductDemo from '../components/ProductDemo.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
import { briefStructure, method, offer } from '../data/offer';
import { briefExcerpt } from '../data/brief-excerpt';
import { dates } from '../lib/benchmark';

const d = dates();
const free = offer.free;
const accountable = [
  { who: 'You', does: 'Own the decision, supply the facts and the constraints, decide what the brief has not decided, and sign the paper. The method will not recommend on a question you have not answered; it records the gap as an unknown.' },
  { who: 'The model', does: 'Reads, asks, drafts and compares at speed. It contributes the analysis. It does not know which fact matters to your organisation until you tell it.' },
  { who: 'Frame', does: 'Holds the model to the process: ask first, tag every material claim, compare real options, state confidence and conditions. It is the discipline, not the judgement.' },
  { who: 'GreenSquare AI', does: 'Writes and maintains the method file, publishes what it has and has not been shown to do, and answers for both. It does not see your decision or your data.' },
];
---
<BaseLayoutV2
  title="Frame | The Decision Brief and the method that produces it"
  description="Frame is a method file for ChatGPT, Claude or another capable model. It makes the model interrogate a consequential decision and produce a Decision Brief with its confidence and conditions stated."
  current="product"
>
  <section class="v-hero product-hero">
    <div class="v-container">
      <h1>The output is a Decision Brief. The method is what makes it defensible.</h1>
      <p class="v-lead">Frame is a plain-text method file you load into the model you already use. It changes what the model does with a consequential decision: it asks before it advises, tags what it is told, compares real options and states the conditions under which its recommendation fails.</p>
      <div class="v-actions">
        <a class="v-btn v-btn--green" href="#get-free">Get the Frame Free beta</a>
        <a class="v-btn" href="#brief">See a Decision Brief</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section" id="brief">
    <div class="v-container">
      <div class="product-head">
        <h2>One decision, read in three states.</h2>
        <p>This is the demonstration run published in the site repository: a fictional 42-branch systems cutover, run once on {briefExcerpt.provenance.model} with the method file that predates Frame, unedited. Move through the question as it was brought, one turn of interrogation, and the brief.</p>
      </div>
      <ProductDemo />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="method">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>The six steps the file holds the model to.</h2>
        <p>The sequence is fixed. What the model asks inside each step depends on what you have already told it, which is why two decisions never produce the same interrogation.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="d-list d-list--indexed">
        {method.map(([name, text], i) => (
          <li><span class="d-list__index">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><div><h3>{name}</h3><p>{text}</p></div></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="receive">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>What you receive.</h2>
        <p>The beta is the method file and nothing else: no application, no account, no upload of your material to GreenSquare AI.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="product-receive">
        <dl class="d-meta">
          <div><dt>The file</dt><dd>{free.delivery.object} {free.delivery.how}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Delivery</dt><dd>{free.delivery.after}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Time</dt><dd>{free.delivery.setup} {free.session}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Compatibility</dt><dd>{free.compatibility.tested} {free.compatibility.boundary}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Your rights</dt><dd>{free.rights}</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="d-panel product-structure">
          <div class="d-panel__head"><strong>Decision Brief</strong><span>structure, as the file produces it</span></div>
          <ol class="product-structure__list">
            {briefStructure.map((row, i) => (
              <li><span class="d-list__index">{i + 1}</span><div><h3>{row.section}</h3><p>{row.carries}</p></div></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <div class="d-panel__foot"><p>Every material claim in the brief is tagged given, derived, inferred or unknown. The brief closes with a confidence statement and what to validate first.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="accountable">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>Who remains accountable.</h2>
        <p>Four parties touch a decision run through Frame. The brief is only as good as the division of labour between them, so it is stated here rather than in the terms.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="d-meta product-accountable">
        {accountable.map((row) => (
          <div><dt>{row.who}</dt><dd>{row.does}</dd></div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="evidence">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>What the evidence covers.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="d-panel product-evidence">
        <dl class="d-meta">
          <div><dt>Shown</dt><dd>In a preregistered benchmark, the method file made the model ask before answering, compare real options and tag its evidence on every run. That is a change in process, and it held across two models and three cases.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Not shown</dt><dd>That the brief is better judged than one a well-briefed model produces unaided. On the three judgement checks the informed baseline matched or exceeded the loaded method.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Boundary</dt><dd>The file tested predates Frame. Nothing on this page claims the benchmark result for Frame Free or Frame Pro. Record current as at {d.currentAsAt}.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="d-panel__foot"><p><a href={withBase('/research/')}>Research overview</a>, <a href={withBase('/benchmark/')}>benchmark record</a> and <a href={withBase('/methodology/')}>methodology</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-section--rule" id="pro">
    <div class="v-container v-cols">
      <div class="v-cols__head">
        <h2>Frame Pro</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="d-panel product-pro">
        <div class="d-panel__head"><strong>{offer.pro.name}</strong><span>{offer.pro.status}</span></div>
        <div class="d-panel__body"><p class="v-small">{offer.pro.note} Until then the Frame Free beta is the only plan, and it is the one this page describes.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Signup />
</BaseLayoutV2>

<style>
  .product-hero h1 { max-width: 20ch; }
  .product-hero .v-lead { max-width: 60ch; }
  .product-head { max-width: 62ch; margin-bottom: var(--v-6); }
  .product-head p { color: var(--v-ink-soft); margin-top: var(--v-4); }
  .product-receive { display: grid; gap: var(--v-6); }
  .product-structure__list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: var(--v-2) var(--v-5); }
  .product-structure__list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; gap: var(--v-3); padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--v-line); }
  .product-structure__list li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .product-structure__list h3 { font-size: 1rem; }
  .product-structure__list p { margin: 2px 0 0; color: var(--v-ink-soft); font-size: var(--vs-small); }
  .product-accountable > div { grid-template-columns: minmax(7rem, 8rem) 1fr; }
  .product-accountable dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--v-ink); font-size: var(--vs-small); }
  .product-evidence { padding: var(--v-2) 0 0; }
  .product-evidence .d-meta { padding: 0 var(--v-5); }
  .product-evidence .d-panel__foot { margin-top: var(--v-2); }
  .product-pro { background: transparent; }
  .product-pro .d-panel__body p { margin: 0; }
</style>
